    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d305">

                <pb facs="0430" n="410" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg410"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/7–1750</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Executive Secretary of the National
                        Security Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the National Security Council
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-07-17">July 17, 1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Future United States Policy With Respect to North
                    Korea</p>
                <p>The President has requested the National Security Council to prepare for his
                    consideration a report on the subject, covering the policy which should be
                    pursued by the United States after the North Korean forces have been driven back
                    to the 38th parallel.</p>
                <p>Accordingly, this project is being referred to the NSC Staff for the preparation of a report for Council
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay,
                            Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
